Third-party notices for the Lozengine binaries
==============================================

Lozengine itself is licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0; see LICENSE-MIT and
LICENSE-APACHE. It has no third-party dependencies: go.mod contains no require
line, and the engine builds against the Go standard library alone.

Any binary built from this repository nevertheless contains parts of the Go
toolchain, listed below with the notices their licenses require: the examples,
the offscreen viewer, and the native library produced by the interoperability
target.

The same file ships with every target. Some components are present only on some
targets; each section says which.


1. The Go standard library and runtime
--------------------------------------

Present in every binary. A Go program is statically linked against the runtime
and against whichever standard library packages it uses — for Lozengine, among
others: image/png, syscall, net, os, sort and math.

